+EQ_Local_Dev, docs/releases/classic-robes-20261022/native-skinning/. Earlier
+candidate/publication records are historical. Native visual acceptance is open.
+
+Classic BAM/BAF, ELM/ELF, HAM/HAF, DWM/DWF, TRM/TRF, OGM/OGF and HOM/HOF now
+have CODE01_DMSPRITEDEF bodies. global4 repeats the Barbarian pair, making16
+registrations. The existing selector at eqgame RVA0x99f0 already chooses robe01.
+The336 original native equip/remove cases mock graphics callbacks and therefore
+do not prove loading or rendering. Keep current proxy/catalog0.11.1 and Classic
+models; no permission, DLL, server, quest, SQL or gameplay-power change here.
+
+build_classic_robes.py runs after canonical HE90 generation and participates in
+client_gameplay_assets.py. Both global archives ship together. Keep palette slots,
+typed-reference relocation and contiguous registrations; preserve original
+fragments/textures, skeletons, animations and helmets. Map Human/Gnome skirts by
+named bones in P01 space; HOF FT0001 is its real feet. NumPy2.4.0 is build-only.
+
+Two independent contracts are necessary. join_waist uses an identical eight-edge
+native bone-local rim and bone IDs, retaining separate UV copies. Distribute
+displacement from hem to rim and around the circumference; rim-only snapping
+inverts faces. Recompute deformed skirt normals and match torso seam normals.
+Then group_vertices_by_bone stably places each bone's vertices in one contiguous
+run, permuting position/UV/normal arrays together and remapping polygon indices.
+This preserves every triangle-corner attribute exactly and adds no geometry.
+
+Pinned EQGraphicsDX9.dll mesh builder0x1004ad50 loops over WLD groups and calls
+ID3DXSkinInfo::SetBoneInfluence at0x1004b4bb. Repeating a bone REPLACES its earlier
+vertex list. Appended skirt runs therefore erased torso/feet assignments. Actual
+x86 d3dx9_30 setter/getter execution loses432 old influences, including181 torso
+waist copies, and zero corrected influences across16 registrations. All168
+decodable stock meshes have unique bone groups. Python/Blender previews expand
+runs independently and masked this defect. Equal saved seams were insufficient.
+
+tools/tests/test_classic_robes.py covers shared seam edges, closed ring, winding,
+unique bone groups and exact preservation. Thirteen tests plus the new actual
+library regression pass; the latter tests all16 corrected models and a split-bone
+negative control. tools/tests/classic_robes_skinning_native.py requires x86 Python
+via NIGHTCAP_X86_PYTHON or the default Python38-32 path and actual d3dx9_30.dll.
+It skips on unsupported hosts. The fixture uses identity vertex remapping;
+native disassembly establishes the same setter after optimizer remapping. This
+is native-library proof, not a complete GPU/game-render or owner acceptance.
